<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mirabel Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Migdal Afek</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mirabel was a crusader castle on the edge of the coastal plain east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffa">Jaffa</a>, at the site now known as Migdal Afek in Israel. Built in the 12th century near the springs of the Yarkon river, it guarded the road from Jaffa to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> and was associated with the lordship of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramla">Ramla</a>, held by the Ibelins. It fell to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> in 1187.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mirabel-castle.jpg" alt="Mirabel Castle" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AVRAM GRAICER · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D7%9E%D7%92%D7%93%D7%9C_%D7%90%D7%A4%D7%A7-%D7%A6%D7%93%D7%A7.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
